103-
104-## Per-chunk execution contract
105-
106-1. Read AGENTS/CLAUDE, glossary, accepted ADRs, the chunk, predecessor receipts,
107-   dependency manifest, test catalogue, and its canonical implementer prompt.
108-2. Confirm a clean approved source snapshot and identify unrelated user work.
109-   Resolve dependency availability/provenance and baseline check limitations.
110-3. Implement only that chunk and approved supporting changes. A shared Academy,
111-   SDK, or Harness change needs its own reviewed revision and regression evidence;
112-   preserve active work and do not move another project's main branch casually.
113-4. Run exact checks from the approved command manifest. Use deterministic local
114-   fixtures and literal external contracts, then the appropriate native tests.
115-   Never call hosted application endpoints by accident.
116-5. Record commands, environments, inputs, results, failures, hashes, limitations,
117-   and rollback rehearsal. Save raw sensitive evidence privately; commit redacted
118-   summaries with references/hashes, not credentials or customer bodies.
119-6. Freeze source and dependency inputs. Request actual independent Codex
120-   review through [the independent prompt](prompts/review-chunk.md) (D026).
